"Custom operators are ordinary two-argument functions"
\infix(11) \blend, ⊕(a,b) = a+b
2 ⊕ 3*4
\blend(2,3)
f = ⊕
f = \blend
\map(f(·,2), ⟨1,2,3⟩)
\eval(\expr(2 ⊕ 3))

"Recursion uses the declared spelling inside the body"
\infix(12) ⊙(a,b) = b <= 0 ? 0 : a + (a ⊙ (b-1))
3 ⊙ 4

"Custom operators associate left; exponentiation associates right"
\infix(15) ⊞(a,b) = a+b
2 ⊞ 3^2
2^3 ⊞ 2

"Punctuation spellings match the longest declared operator"
\infix(11) \merge, <+>(a,b) = a+b
2<+>3*4
<+>(2,3)
g=<+>
g=\merge
\infix(11) ~(a,b) = a-b
\infix(11) ~~(a,b) = a+b
10~~3~2

"Sections fix either operand using ordinary partial application"
(2 ⊕)(3)
(⊕ 2)(3)
\map((<+> 2), ⟨1,2,3⟩)
(\merge 2)(3)
(<+> 2*3)(10)
(<+> (2,3))
<+>(·,(1+2))(10)
\expr((<+> 2))
\eval(\expr((2 <+>)))(3)
